## Issue 1 — Obstacle Avoidance: Multi-Phase State Machine

### Before (original logic)
```
if obstacle < 0.5m:
    turn in place          ← robot oscillates / gets stuck
else:
    move forward if RSSI improving
```

### After — `AvoidPhase` enum with 5 states

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> CLEAR : startup
    CLEAR --> BACK : obstacle < 0.5 m detected
    BACK --> ARC : 0.8 s elapsed\n(reverse at –0.15 m/s)
    ARC --> VERIFY : 1.5 s elapsed\n(arc turn ±0.5 rad/s + 0.1 m/s fwd)
    VERIFY --> RESUME : path clear after 0.5 s
    VERIFY --> BACK : still blocked → flip threat side
    RESUME --> CLEAR : RSSI reference synced
```

| Phase | Duration | linear.x | angular.z | Purpose |
|-------|----------|----------|-----------|---------|
| `BACK` | 0.8 s | −0.15 m/s | 0 | Reverse to gain clearance |
| `ARC` | 1.5 s | +0.10 m/s | ±0.5 rad/s | Arc away from threat side |
| `VERIFY` | 0.5 s | +0.08 m/s | 0 | Creep-check path is clear |
| `RESUME` | instant | 0 | 0 | Sync RSSI reference → CLEAR |

**Anti-oscillation:** `_threat_side` alternates `'left'` ↔ `'right'` on each re-block, so the robot arcs the other way if the first escape attempt fails.

